                    "content": "Here's my recommendation for a French restaurant open on Sunday in Paris:\n\n**Breizh Caf\u00e9** \u2b50\n\n- **Rating:** 3.9\n- **Address:** 109 Rue Vieille du Temple, 75003 Paris, France\n- **Operating Hours:** 9:00 AM \u2013 11:00 PM (open on Mondays, Tuesdays, Thursdays, Fridays, Saturdays, and Sundays)\n\n**Note:** Among the French restaurants in Paris, Breizh Caf\u00e9 is the **only one open on Sunday**. The other French options (Le Baratin, Bistrot Paul Bert, and Chez L'Ami Jean) are all closed on Sundays, so despite having higher ratings, they aren't available for your arrival day.\n\nBreizh Caf\u00e9 is known for its excellent sweet and savory crepes (including gluten-free buckwheat options), authentic Breton cider, and friendly staff. Do note it's a busy spot, so expect a wait during peak hours. Enjoy your trip to Paris!"
